# Rust / Tauri
#
# `target/` unanchored, not `src-tauri/target/`: each crate under
# src-tauri/crates/ builds into its own target/ when it is built standalone
# (cargo test -p, or before the workspace existed), and an anchored rule misses
# every one of them. That is 140 MB of object files into the first commit.
target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Release artefacts. Built by scripts/release-local.sh and attached to the
# GitHub release; they do not belong in the history.
dist-release/

# The generated iOS project. `tauri ios init` recreates it in full and nothing
# in it is hand written -- persistent plist keys live in src-tauri/Info.plist,
# which Tauri merges.
src-tauri/gen/apple/

# gen/android/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Tauri has no configuration field
# for Android permissions, so RECORD_AUDIO can only be declared by editing the
# generated AndroidManifest.xml -- and a meter that cannot open the microphone
# is the entire app. Tauri ships its own .gitignore files inside the directory
# that exclude the build output, jniLibs and local.properties, which is why
# tracking it costs about forty small files rather than a Gradle tree.
#
# `tauri android init` overwrites the manifest. If you ever re-run it, put
# RECORD_AUDIO back.
